  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>SN1 reaction mechanism follows a step-by-step process wherein first, the carbocation is formed from the removal of the leaving group. Then the carbocation is attacked by the nucleophile.</p><p>tertiary, benzylic or allylic carbocations are stable carbocations So, they can give this reaction.</p><p>But Bridge head carbocation formed in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>SN</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math>pathway is unstable. So, option (C) does not give this reaction.</p>",
